<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43538" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēmĭ-pēs</span></b> ,
			pĕdis, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A half-foot</i>, <i>half a foot.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> As a measure of length,
					<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 123</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 3, 5, 15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">latum semipede,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 2,
					3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">minimi semipedum mensura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 5, 4, § 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non altiores quino semipede,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					17, 11, 16, § 80</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intervallo duum pedum et semipedis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					17, 20, 33, § 144</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A half-foot</i> in verse, Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 18,
				15, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 4, 86</span></i>; Aug.
			de Musica, 5, 11.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Half-lame</i>: crure trunco semipes, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεΦ.</span> 2, 150.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
